1
00:00:02,872 --> 00:00:07,872
== sync, corrected by elderman ==
@elder_man

2
00:00:07,873 --> 00:00:10,503
(Bernadette:)I'm worried about Howard.
Ever since that guy

3
00:00:10,508 --> 00:00:12,738
(Bernadette:)from the Air Force showed up,
he's been a nervous wreck.

4
00:00:12,743 --> 00:00:14,743
(Penny:)All right, we work at
a giant pharmaceutical company.

5
00:00:14,745 --> 00:00:16,475
(Penny:)Get him some anti-anxiety meds.

6
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:18,350
(Bernadette:)He won't take any pills
that aren't chewable

7
00:00:18,349 --> 00:00:20,419
(Bernadette:)and shaped like a Flintstone.

8
00:00:20,418 --> 00:00:22,788
(Penny:)You know, when Leonard's
feeling anxious

9
00:00:22,787 --> 00:00:24,217
(Penny:)I make him take a long walk.

10
00:00:24,221 --> 00:00:25,291
(Amy:)Does that help?

11
00:00:25,289 --> 00:00:28,219
(Penny:)Well, for a while.
Then he comes back.

12
00:00:29,393 --> 00:00:30,863
(Bernadette:)I don't believe this.

13
00:00:30,890 --> 00:00:31,560
(Amy:)What's wrong?

14
00:00:31,562 --> 00:00:33,932
(Bernadette:)This guy from the office
just congratulated me

15
00:00:33,931 --> 00:00:35,461
(Bernadette:)on being pregnant.

16
00:00:35,466 --> 00:00:37,636
(Amy:)You did already know, right?

17
00:00:38,469 --> 00:00:40,699
(Bernadette:)No one at the office did.

18
00:00:40,705 --> 00:00:41,835
(Bernadette:)Did you tell
anyone?

19
00:00:41,862 --> 00:00:43,372
(Raj:)No.
You told me not to.

20
00:00:43,375 --> 00:00:45,345
(Bernadette:)I bet it was Barbara Chen
in retrovirus.

21
00:00:45,342 --> 00:00:47,572
(Bernadette:)She might have heard me
throwing up one morning.

22
00:00:47,578 --> 00:00:48,808
(Bernadette:)Every since she got

23
00:00:48,813 --> 00:00:51,943
(Bernadette:)the hearing aid,
she thinks she's so great.

24
00:00:52,817 --> 00:00:55,287
(Amy:)Why don't you want
anyone to know?

25
00:00:55,286 --> 00:00:57,016
'Cause I'm up for a major
immunotherapy study,

26
00:00:57,021 --> 00:00:58,621
(Bernadette:)and if they find out
I'm pregnant

27
00:00:58,622 --> 00:01:00,322
(Bernadette:)they might give it
to someone else.

28
00:01:00,324 --> 00:01:01,654
(Penny:)Would they really do that?

